### 1. GET ALL CATS
GET http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/cats

### 2. CREATE A NEW CAT
POST http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/cats HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=MyBoundary

--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="cat_name"

Misu
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="weight"

6
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="owner"

37
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="birthdate"

2023-10-08
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="cat"; filename="dog.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./dog.jpg
--MyBoundary--

### GET CATS BY USER ID
GET http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/cats/user/37   

### CREATE A NEW USER
POST http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Aubhav Rimal",
  "username": "anubhavr",
  "email": "anubhavr@test.com",
  "password": "mySuperSecretPassword123"
}

### LOGIN USER
# @name login
POST http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "anubhavr",
  "password": "mySuperSecretPassword123"
}

### GET MY USER INFO (Protected Route)
GET http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### TEST 1: Regular user tries to update another user's cat (Should return 403 Forbidden)
# Logged in as User 38 (anubhavr), trying to edit Cat 41 (owned by User 37)
PUT http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/cats/41
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cat_name": "Hacked Cat"
}

### TEST 2: Regular user tries to update another user's profile (Should return 403 Forbidden)
# Logged in as User 38, trying to modify User 37
PUT http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/users/37
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Intruder"
}

### TEST VALIDATION: Try to create a user with bad data
POST http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rule Breaker",
  "username": "ha", 
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123"
}